From 2ab7eb70a62933cd136eea17ea4046b1d2b38b28 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 09:11:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Rebuild the page as one continuous scroll-driven 3D take
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The hero's contained node network becomes a full-page world: a fixed canvas
behind the document, with scroll position driving a camera through eight beats
— a single node in a small room, the question that breaks it apart, the lattice
it snaps into, the lens it grows, the benchmark it locks off on, the region it
replicates across, the system that ends up in production, and the pull-out that
returns it to one light.

There are no cuts. Every beat is the same ~1800 points in a different
arrangement, so a morph is a lerp between two position sets rather than a scene
swap, and the node that opens the take is the node that closes it.

- beats.js: the shot list — eight shapes, each with its camera, node scale,
  edge opacity, drift rate and framing offset.
- world.js: the rig — tier detection, scroll driver, damped camera, and a
  render loop that stops once nothing is left to settle.

Notes on the implementation:

- Scroll is never intercepted. The canvas is fixed, takes no pointer events,
  and the document scrolls over it exactly as before.
- Three draw calls for the whole world. Instance buffers are only rewritten
  when the morph advances; MEASUREMENT drifts at zero, so a camera parked
  there renders nothing.
- r185's fragment shader only applies vColor under USE_COLOR, so instanceColor
  alone is silently dropped. An all-white vertex colour attribute on the base
  geometry turns it on and leaves instanceColor as the only thing tinting a node.
- Three tiers: full on desktop, reduced geometry and no idle drift on phones,
  and off entirely for reduced motion or missing WebGL — which restores exactly
  the previous flat site, static hero SVG included.
- The journey and proof panels fade in and out rather than starting hard; over
  a continuous shot a solid panel edge reads as a seam.
- shots.mjs takes CHROMIUM_PATH so a CI image can point at a browser Playwright
  did not download itself.

Verified at 1440, 1280, 820, 390 and 320px: no horizontal overflow, no console
errors, and the world composes clear of the copy at every width.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
